tests/ir/specialize_sign.sky:16:7: note: [SPEC-001] specialized `g` for x > 0 at this call: 0 checks removed
   |
16 | print(g(abs(z) + 1), g(-1 - abs(z)), h(abs(z) + 1))
   |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: applied by the `specialize` pass
   = note: because 0 run-time checks removed: operations that can fail in `g` and cannot in `g[x>0]`
   = note: because the argument for `x` is positive (at least 1)
   = note: because in `g[x>0]`: 1 comparison decided by the sign, 2 branches decided, 1 operation folded to constants
   = note: because the specialization is the same code with these values known: outputs, errors and their spans are unchanged

